   "source": [
    "# FRADO Python — Google Colab demonstration\n",
<div align="center">
  <img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/naddaf-AGN/frado-python/main/assets/frado_logo.png"
       width="300">
</div>
    "\n",
    "[![Open in Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/assets/colab-badge.svg)](https://colab.research.google.com/github/naddaf-AGN/frado-python/blob/main/examples/FRADO_Colab_Demo.ipynb)\n",
    "\n",
    "**FRADO Python v1.0.0** · [Source code](https://github.com/naddaf-AGN/frado-python) · [Software DOI](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23442013)\n",
    "\n",
    "Run a small sweep of three dusty-cloud launch radii **entirely in Google Colab**, inspect the outcomes, plot a trajectory, and download the results. **No Python installation on your computer is needed.**\n",
    "\n",
    "Choose **Runtime → Run all**. The initial Numba compilation and numerical integrations can take some time. Use a standard CPU runtime.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Scientific scope:** This is a demonstration, not a validation across all AGN parameter space. Consult the [validation notes](https://github.com/naddaf-AGN/frado-python/blob/main/docs/VALIDATION.md) before scientific interpretation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b0793ead",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1 · Retrieve the official source release\n",
    "\n",
    "The source is fetched directly from GitHub, **pinned to the `v1.0.0` tag** for reproducibility."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "810acdad",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import subprocess\n",
    "\n",
    "repo = Path('/content/frado-python-v1.0.0')\n",
    "if not repo.exists():\n",
    "    subprocess.run([\n",
    "        'git', 'clone', '--branch', 'v1.0.0', '--depth', '1',\n",
    "        'https://github.com/naddaf-AGN/frado-python.git', str(repo)\n",
    "    ], check=True)\n",
    "os.chdir(repo)\n",
    "commit = subprocess.check_output(['git', 'rev-parse', '--short', 'HEAD'], text=True).strip()\n",
    "print(f'FRADO Python v1.0.0 — commit {commit}; directory: {repo}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "64f8994f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2 · Install required packages in Colab\n",
    "\n",
    "This changes only the temporary cloud runtime, not your local computer."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "905e46f5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%pip install -q -r requirements-optimized.txt"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "84e32f48",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3 · Simulate three launch radii\n",
    "\n",
    "The supplied example uses **Numba-accelerated adaptive radiation quadrature** and launch radii **8370, 8380, and 8390 Rg**. Each run writes physical outputs plus numerical-diagnostic information."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "fab2e465",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "subprocess.run([\n",
    "    sys.executable, 'run.py', '--config', 'examples/optimized_sweep.json',\n",
    "    '--output-dir', 'OutPut/colab_demo', '--on-error', 'raise'\n",
    "], check=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cccbe337",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4 · Examine the run summary\n",
    "\n",
    "The numerical-status column indicates whether any numerical quality flags require closer examination."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "96cc769d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from IPython.display import display\n",
    "\n",
    "outdir = repo / 'OutPut/colab_demo'\n",
    "summary = pd.read_csv(outdir / 'summary.csv')\n",
    "cols = ['launch_radius_rg', 'termination_reason', 'flight_time_years',\n",
    "        'max_z_rg_sampled', 'numerical_status']\n",
    "display(summary[cols])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1396db21",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5 · Visualize a cloud trajectory\n",
    "\n",
    "This plot shows **cylindrical distance from the symmetry axis** versus **height above the disk midplane** for the first saved trajectory. It does not by itself assess physical validity."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "655ff3bd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "saved = summary.dropna(subset=['trajectory_file'])\n",
    "if saved.empty:\n",
    "    raise RuntimeError('No trajectory was saved. Inspect summary.csv and launch_screening.csv.')\n",
    "trajectory_path = repo / str(saved.iloc[0]['trajectory_file'])\n",
    "array = np.loadtxt(trajectory_path, comments='#', ndmin=2)\n",
    "rho_rg = np.hypot(array[:, 1], array[:, 2])\n",
    "z_rg = array[:, 3]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7, 4.5))\n",
    "ax.plot(rho_rg, z_rg, lw=1.5)\n",
    "ax.plot(rho_rg[0], z_rg[0], 'o', label='Launch point')\n",
    "ax.set(xlabel=r'Cylindrical radius $\\rho$ [$R_\\mathrm{g}$]',\n",
    "       ylabel=r'Height $z$ [$R_\\mathrm{g}$]',\n",
    "       title=f'FRADO trajectory: launch at {saved.iloc[0][\"launch_radius_rg\"]:g} Rg')\n",
    "ax.grid(alpha=0.3)\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d131dcdc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6 · Download all results\n",
    "\n",
    "Colab runtimes are temporary. Save the output archive if you want to keep your computed data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a38af3a1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import shutil\n",
    "from google.colab import files\n",
    "\n",
    "archive_path = shutil.make_archive('/content/frado_v1_0_0_colab_results', 'zip',\n",
    "                                   root_dir=outdir.parent, base_dir=outdir.name)\n",
    "files.download(archive_path)"
   ]
  },
